==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|en|strong form}}:
** {{IPA|en|/æt/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-at.ogg|a=US}}
** {{rhymes|en|æt|s=1}}
* {{a|en|weak form}}:
** {{IPA|en|/ət/}}
** {{hmp|en|it<q:some accents>}}
* {{hmp|en|at}}

===Etymology 1===

====Preposition====
{{en-head|prep}}

# [[at|At]] a rate of (so much each).
#: {{ux|en|15 items '''@''' $10}}
#: {{uxi|en|'''@''' 80 km/h|at eighty kilometres per hour}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[at|At]] (any sense).
#: {{uxi|en|'''@''' 20°C|at twenty degrees Celsius}}
#: {{ux|en|Text message: “im '''@''' school.”}}

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|at a rate of}}
* Catalan:
* Danish:
* Dutch:
* German:
* Hungarian:
* Norwegian:
* Swedish:
{{trans-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|Internet slang|transitive}} To reply to or speak to someone, either online or face to face. {{q|from the practice of targeting a message or reply to someone online by writing @''name''}}
#: {{ux|en|Honestly, don't '''@''' me if you don't have anything nice to say.}}
#: {{ux|en|He angrily '''@ed''' me after I made an innocent comment.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023|author={{w|R. F. Kuang}}|title=[[w:Yellowface (novel)|Yellowface]]|publisher=The Borough Press|page=2|passage=She regularly tweets career updates and quirky jokes to her seventy thousand followers, but she rarely '''@'''s other people.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Chiefly used in the phrase {{m|en|don't @ me}}. It can be used humorously when stated after an unpopular or ironic opinion, in order to forestall dissent.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Internet slang}} The permanent [[handle]] of a user which follows @, chiefly on Twitter.
#: {{ux|en|What your @?}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|at#Verb|at}}

====See also====
* [[at sign]]
* {{l|en|@ party}}
* {{l|en|@mention}}

===Etymology 2===
{{-a-o-@|en}}

====Symbol====
{{en-head|sym}}

# {{senseid|en|gender}}{{n-g|Forming gender-neutral versions of Spanish-derived words by replacing both the masculine ''-o'' and feminine ''-a''.}}
#: {{co|en|[[Chican@]], [[Filipin@]], [[Latin@]], [[Mestiz@]]}}
# {{n-g|By extension, sometimes used to blend other pairs of words that differ by being spelled with ''o'' vs ''a''.}}
#: {{co|en|[[Kosov@]]; [[Pin@y]]}}

====See also====
* [[x#en-gender|x]]

===Etymology 3===
{{bor+|en|ms|@}}, abbreviation of {{der|en|ms|atau|t=or}}.

====Symbol====
{{en-head|sym}}

# {{lb|en|Singapore|Malaysia}} {{n-g|Connecting a [[person]]'s [[common name]] and [[alias]], both of them are [[legal name]]s.}}
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Tan Cheng Bock}} '''@''' Adrian Tan}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|en|conjunction}}

# {{lb|en|Malaysia|informal}} [[or]]
#: {{ux|en|Apples '''@''' oranges}}

==Russian==

===Symbol===
{{head|ru|symbol}}

# {{rfd-sense|sv}} {{l|mul|@}}

====Usage notes====
* This symbol is called {{m|ru|эт}}, {{m|ru|лягу́шка}}, {{m|ru|обезья́нка}}, {{m|ru|соба́ка}}, or {{m|ru|[[коммерческий|комме́рческое]] «[[эт]]»}}.
